====================================================================
FORKS = 2 , SERIAL = 8
HOW DOES ANSIBLE EXECUTE?
====================================================================

Suppose you have

16 Servers

S1 S2 S3 S4 S5 S6 S7 S8
S9 S10 S11 S12 S13 S14 S15 S16


Configuration

forks = 2

serial = 8


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 1
--------------------------------------------------

Serial selects the first batch:

S1 S2 S3 S4 S5 S6 S7 S8

(8 servers)


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 2
--------------------------------------------------

Forks = 2

Means Ansible can execute tasks on
only 2 servers simultaneously.

Execution:

Round 1

S1   S2

↓

Round 2

S3   S4

↓

Round 3

S5   S6

↓

Round 4

S7   S8

The first batch is complete.


--------------------------------------------------
STEP 3
--------------------------------------------------

Serial now moves to next batch

S9 S10 S11 S12 S13 S14 S15 S16


Again,

Forks = 2

Execution

Round 1

S9   S10

↓

Round 2

S11  S12

↓

Round 3

S13  S14

↓

Round 4

S15  S16

Done.

