====================================================================
ANSIBLE VAULT
====================================================================

--------------------------------------------------
WHAT IS ANSIBLE VAULT?
--------------------------------------------------

Ansible Vault is a security feature used
to encrypt sensitive information.

Examples:

    • Passwords
    • API Keys
    • AWS Access Keys
    • Secret Keys
    • Database Passwords
    • SSL Certificates

Encrypted data can only be viewed
using the correct Vault Password.


====================================================================
WHY DO WE NEED ANSIBLE VAULT?
====================================================================

Problem:

Suppose your playbook contains

------------------------------------

db_password: admin123

aws_secret_key: ABCXYZ123

------------------------------------

If stored in GitHub,

Anyone can see the passwords ❌


Solution

Encrypt the file using
Ansible Vault.

Now the file looks like

------------------------------------

$ANSIBLE_VAULT;1.1;AES256

6634656534...

------------------------------------

No one can read it without
the vault password.


====================================================================
REAL-TIME USE CASE
====================================================================

Company uses GitHub.

Repository contains

Playbooks

↓

Variables

↓

Database Password

↓

AWS Credentials

Instead of storing them
as plain text,

Encrypt them using
Ansible Vault.


====================================================================
HOW ANSIBLE VAULT WORKS
====================================================================

Plain Text Variables

        ↓

ansible-vault encrypt

        ↓

Encrypted File

        ↓

Git Repository

        ↓

During Playbook Execution

Provide Vault Password

        ↓

Ansible decrypts automatically


====================================================================
COMMON VAULT COMMANDS
====================================================================

--------------------------------------------------
1. CREATE ENCRYPTED FILE
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault create secrets.yml

You will be asked

Vault Password:

Confirm Vault Password:

Now edit the file.


--------------------------------------------------
2. VIEW ENCRYPTED FILE
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault view secrets.yml


--------------------------------------------------
3. EDIT ENCRYPTED FILE
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault edit secrets.yml


--------------------------------------------------
4. ENCRYPT EXISTING FILE
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault encrypt secrets.yml


--------------------------------------------------
5. DECRYPT FILE
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault decrypt secrets.yml


--------------------------------------------------
6. CHANGE VAULT PASSWORD
--------------------------------------------------

ansible-vault rekey secrets.yml


====================================================================
EXAMPLE
====================================================================

Create

secrets.yml

Contains

------------------------------------

db_user: admin

db_password: MyPassword123

------------------------------------

Encrypt

ansible-vault encrypt secrets.yml


Now

Nobody can read the file.


====================================================================
USING VAULT IN PLAYBOOK
====================================================================

Playbook

------------------------------------

- hosts: web

  vars_files:

    - secrets.yml

  tasks:

  - debug:

      msg: "{{ db_password }}"

------------------------------------

Run

ansible-playbook app.yml \
--ask-vault-pass


Ansible asks

Vault Password:

After entering the correct password,

Playbook executes successfully.


====================================================================
USING VAULT PASSWORD FILE
====================================================================

Instead of typing password every time,

Create

vault_pass.txt

Contains

------------------------------------

MyVaultPassword

------------------------------------

Run

ansible-playbook app.yml \
--vault-password-file vault_pass.txt

Useful for

CI/CD pipelines.


====================================================================
REAL DEVOPS USE CASE
====================================================================

Jenkins

↓

Runs Playbook

↓

Uses Vault Password File

↓

Decrypts Secrets

↓

Deploys Application


No passwords exposed.


====================================================================
WHAT CAN BE ENCRYPTED?
====================================================================

• Variable Files

• Playbooks

• Individual Variables

• Entire YAML Files


====================================================================
ENCRYPT SINGLE VARIABLE
====================================================================

Generate encrypted string

ansible-vault encrypt_string \
'MyPassword123' \
--name 'db_password'

Output

------------------------------------

db_password: !vault |

$ANSIBLE_VAULT;1.1;AES256

xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

------------------------------------

Useful when only one variable
needs encryption.


====================================================================
BEST PRACTICES
====================================================================

✓ Encrypt only sensitive data

✓ Store vault password separately

✓ Never commit vault password
  to Git

✓ Use Jenkins Credentials
  for vault password

✓ Rotate vault passwords regularly


====================================================================
ANSIBLE VAULT vs JENKINS CREDENTIALS
====================================================================

Ansible Vault

    Encrypts files and variables.

Jenkins Credentials

    Securely stores passwords,
    tokens and secrets inside Jenkins.

Often used together.


====================================================================
INTERVIEW QUESTIONS
====================================================================

Q1. What is Ansible Vault?

Answer:

Ansible Vault is a feature used to
encrypt sensitive data such as passwords,
API keys and credentials so they can be
stored securely in playbooks or variable files.


--------------------------------------------------

Q2. Why do we need Vault?

To prevent sensitive information from
being exposed in source code repositories.


--------------------------------------------------

Q3. Which encryption algorithm is used?

AES-256


--------------------------------------------------

Q4. How do you execute a playbook
using Vault?

ansible-playbook app.yml \
--ask-vault-pass

or

ansible-playbook app.yml \
--vault-password-file vault_pass.txt


--------------------------------------------------

Q5. Where is Vault commonly used?

• GitHub

• GitLab

• Jenkins

• AWS Automation

• Production deployments


